    <GaugingStation location="Temple" name="Lark" number="33014">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Compound broad-crested weir gauging a Chalk catchment with significant artificial influences.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Not drowned at 1.8m stage. One rating applied across period of record, full range rating confirmed by current meter measurements.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Compound broad-crested weir with rectangular cross-section, 5.8m broad, central notch 3m broad.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Flows affected by milling u/s of gauging station. Significant groundwater abstractions in catchment for PWS, industry and agriculture. Some effluent returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly Chalk overlain with Boulder Clay. Agricultural land use.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">GEI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Within modular range and flows contained." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to within 3% of AMAX3. Within modular range and flows contained although highest gauging does deviate slightly from rating." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
